## Accessibility Requirements (WCAG 2.2 AA)

### Critical Accessibility Features
1. **Keyboard Navigation**: All interactive elements accessible via keyboard
2. **Screen Reader Support**: Proper ARIA labels and semantic HTML
3. **Color Contrast**: 4.5:1 minimum ratio for normal text, 3:1 for large text
4. **Focus Management**: Clear focus indicators and logical tab order
5. **Error Handling**: Clear error messages with correction guidance
6. **Responsive Design**: Usable at 400% zoom level

### Implementation Requirements
```typescript
// Example accessible button component
<Button
  className="min-h-[44px] min-w-[44px]" // WCAG touch target size
  aria-label="Vote Yes on Proposal 123"
  disabled={isSubmitting}
  aria-describedby="vote-help-text"
>
  {isSubmitting ? (
    <>
      <Loader2 className="mr-2 h-4 w-4 animate-spin" />
      <span className="sr-only">Submitting vote...</span>
      Submitting
    </>
